d officials as we're learning  Barack Obama was slammed for his  relatively modest vacation days and then  Trump setting records in terms of the  number of days he's taking off and the  cost of those golf trips it contradicts  what Trump said he would do during the  campaign he said he'd be at the White  House all the time he  be working working with no brakes and  Republicans don't even care that he's  doing the exact opposite and I was  thinking about this and you know the  obvious double standard and there is a  really big one but you can't even talk  to Republicans about double standards  anymore if you bring up the double  standard of trumps vacation time if you  bring up the double standard of Trump  exploding the deficit while claiming he  would fix it and criticizing others for  the debt and deficit or whatever else  there's a deeper problem here which is  that even if you can point out a double  standard on a particular issue much of  the American right has bought into the  idea that problems aren't complex that  problems are simple and that the  solutions are simple and that you don't  really need a president who studies and  reads and consults and learns they have  bought in hook line and sinker to the  idea that you just need someone with the  right seven-word talking point build a  wall band trans people from the military  bail on Syria cut taxes and Obama care  whatever it is and when you believe that  solutions are as simple as the American  right believes that they are you no  longer care about double standards by  the president you no longer care about a  president who doesn't read or spend time  learning about any of these issues and  that's it okay  it's a worldview that's not based in  reality and it underlies this entire  sort of small government [ __ ]  presidents are okay industrial complex  which we saw first with george w bush  that was nothing compared to what we're  seeing under donald trump bush at least  read the wrong stuff I'm not  romanticizing george w bush but at least  he read and listened to advisors they  were horrible right-wing neocon Warhawk  advisors but he at least handled this in  a more reasonable way in the back of  this there is this underlying issue of  Republicans buying this ruse that the  solutions are always really simple and  also when you hear that Donald Trump is  just wandering out to go watch TV I mean  that's the type of  you think about when you are aware of  someone's cognitive decline so this of  course continuing to raise more  questions and concerns for people on the  Left people in the middle and on the  right who are sort of connected to the  realities of what we should expect from  a president but if you believe that all  the answers are simple and you think  that as long as you've got the right  single talking point nothing else  matters you're probably not going to be  hugely concerned by this revelation  today's program is sponsored in part by  Blink asam / Pakman if you've not  already heard about blink Asst it's  amazing it's an app for your phone  tablet or web browser and what they do  is they take nonfiction books popular  nonfiction critically acclaimed  nonfiction they condense the book into a  fifteen minute audio book you get all  the most important information and  insights from each book but you can soak  up the entire essence of the book in one  sitting I've listened to a ton of books  on blinkin recent one is a Robert Rice's  new book the common good also bunk by  Kevin Young useful in preparing me for  the pseudo-science miniseries that we're  producing and if you are a david pakman  show viewer or listener you can get a  seven day free trial by going to blink  is comm slash Pakman if you're watching  on youtube use the link in the video  description  after the free trial if you like it you  can get the full access to thousands of  condensed audiobooks for about five  bucks a month that's be li NK is t.com  /pa ke ma n
 

